in after v1 -- a firearm received from another licensee, or the exportRecord on Invari's ledger -- and its first previousEntryHash then points to an entry outside this file (join it with the previous holder's export).","6. masterRootHash = SHA-256 of every ledger section's rootHash followed by every record section's rootHash, each group in the order the sections appear in this file (kernel/tools/verifyExport.js applies this rule).","7. Signed records: a record in affirmationArtifacts or enforcementLog with sealFormatVersion 2 (3 for a chained affirmation) verifies like a ledger entry -- SHA-256 of its domain ('invari.kos.affirmation.record.v1' or 'invari.kos.enforcement.record.v1'), a newline, then the canonical form of the record without _id, entryHash and entrySignature; then its entrySignature with the published key for signingKeyId. A record without sealFormatVersion was written under an older, unsigned formula and verifies only by that (kernel/tools/verifyExport.js reports it as legacy).","8. Affirmation chains (3.3.0): a record with sealFormatVersion 3 verifies as in 7 and is also a link in its subject's chain (assetId). Group by assetId, sort by chainSequence: numbered 1..n with no gap, each previousRecordHash equal to the prior record's entryHash (null on the first), one subjectType, createdAt never decreasing, and every RETRACT naming an earlier AFFIRM of the same nodeRef. This file carries the whole chain of every subject a ledger entry cites; a cited affirmation must be its gate's latest record at the citing entry's eventTimestamp."],"note":"Ledger entries and signed records verify with only Invari's public key; no Invari infrastructure is required."},"exportEntryHash":"a34c3489b5bbb859c5691fe07d620d9461bf55cd88e9af82ae566210417f6378","exportEntryVersion":5},"entityChain":{"rootHash":"ac2690dab65d00fbc819bcf38675d69541b9b0650445cc2da87669fb5d91f914","entryCount":5,"entries":[{"_id":{"$oid":"6af13ae1061a867dcfe13330"},"assetId":"entity::6af13ae1061a867dcfe